{"id":"apa6","name":"apa6","aliases":[],"caption":"Format documents in APA style (6th edition)","authors":[{"id":"beitzel","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Brian D. Beitzel","year":"2011-2023"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"2.35","date":"2023-08-07"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      The class formats documents in APA style (6th Edition). It\n      provides a full set of facilities in three different output modes\n      (journal-like appearance, double-spaced manuscript, LaTeX-like\n      document), in contrast to the earlier\n      <ref refid=\"apa6e\">apa6e<\u002fref>, which only formats double-spaced\n      manuscripts in APA style. The class can mask author identity for\n      copies for use in masked peer review.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      The class is a development of\n      the <ref refid=\"apa\">apa<\u002fref> class (which is no longer\n      maintained).\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/apa6/README"},{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/apa6/apa6.pdf"}],"ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/apa6","file":true},"miktex":"apa6","texlive":"apa6","topics":["journalpub","psychology","class","apa"]}